{
  "_comment": "Search keywords. Morphology is solved here, by hand, not by a stemmer on the client. Titles are indexed automatically — this file only adds what a title does not contain: abbreviations, slang, spelling variants, alternative names. Keys are `{type}.{id}`. Read by the rule matcher in scripts/lib/rules.ts as well as by search, in every language at once: a phrase here can bind a playlist to this course on its own. Slang that is a different subject's ordinary word — «inheritance», «feedback» — costs a wrong binding, so add loose synonyms knowing they are load-bearing. A value written with a leading `?` is search-only: search finds the course by it, the matcher never binds a playlist on it. That is for words that are a good guess in a search box and a wrong answer as a rule — «genre» is not a course, but «Ambient Music Playlist | Genre» covers that clause exactly.",
